{"text":"In preparation for this address, I was pleasantly surprised to learn how far back Liberia's connection to Harvard goes. The establishment in 1862 of Liberia College, now the University of Liberia, the second oldest institution of higher learning in West Africa, was led and funded by the Trustees of Donation for Education in Liberia. Simon Greenfield, the Harvard College Law Professor who drafted Liberia's Independence Constitution of 1847, was the founder and president of that institution, which is still in existence today. The first Liberian graduate of Harvard did so in 1920, and since then, there has been a steady trail of Liberians to Cambridge, over 30, to my count. Most of them returned home to pursue successful careers.","words":[{"text":"In","start":0.0,"end":1.26},{"text":"preparation","start":1.26,"end":1.62},{"text":"for","start":1.62,"end":2.14},{"text":"this","start":2.14,"end":2.34},{"text":"address","start":2.34,"end":2.84,"punct":","},{"text":"I","start":4.94,"end":5.16},{"text":"was","start":5.16,"end":5.32},{"text":"pleasantly","start":5.32,"end":5.86},{"text":"surprised","start":5.86,"end":6.58},{"text":"to","start":6.58,"end":8.06},{"text":"learn","start":8.06,"end":8.28},{"text":"how","start":8.28,"end":8.6},{"text":"far","start":8.6,"end":8.94},{"text":"back","start":8.94,"end":9.34},{"text":"Liberia's","start":9.34,"end":10.08},{"text":"connection","start":10.08,"end":10.4},{"text":"to","start":10.4,"end":10.74},{"text":"Harvard","start":10.74,"end":11.02},{"text":"goes","start":11.02,"end":11.46,"punct":"."},{"text":"The","start":12.76,"end":13.08},{"text":"establishment","start":13.08,"end":13.58},{"text":"in","start":13.58,"end":13.92},{"text":"1862","start":13.92,"end":14.8},{"text":"of","start":14.8,"end":16.34},{"text":"Liberia","start":16.34,"end":16.76},{"text":"College","start":16.76,"end":17.48,"punct":","},{"text":"now","start":18.62,"end":18.8},{"text":"the","start":18.8,"end":18.96},{"text":"University","start":18.96,"end